<title>USA: Northwest Q2 cargo traffic flat, yield up.</title>
<headline>Northwest Q2 cargo traffic flat, yield up.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northwest Airlines said its second quarter cargo traffic was flat, but revenues rose 5.3 percent on the strength of higher yields.</p>
<p>&quot;Our cargo operations performed well, posting substantial increases in unit revenue,&quot; said president and chief executive John Dasburg.</p>
<p>Second quarter cargo ton miles eased up 0.3 percent, to 553.6 million in 1997 from 555.1 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>Cargo revenue per ton mile rose 5.6 percent - to 35.39 cents from 33.51 in the second quarter last year.</p>
</text>
